  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large 12 inch skillet with a lid over medium-high heat. Add the onion and sweet potatoes.",
    "Cook for 5 minutes, stirring now and then, until the edges start to brown.",
    "Push the vegetables to the sides. Add the turkey to the center and break it up with a spoon.",
    "Stir in the garlic, cumin, smoked paprika, salt, and pepper. Cook for 4 minutes, until the turkey is no longer pink.",
    "Pour in the water and scrape up any browned bits. Cover and cook for 4 minutes, until the sweet potatoes are nearly tender.",
    "Add the kale in handfuls and stir until it wilts. Cover and cook 2 more minutes.",
    "Check that the turkey reads 165 F and a sweet potato cube is soft when pierced with a fork. Serve hot, or cool and refrigerate for up to 4 days."
  ],
